## 13. Implementation roadmap

### First 90 days: build the operating foundation

- Select initial grades and subjects rather than localizing the entire US catalog;
- Document global product invariants;
- Establish the global and national governance councils;
- Map legal, curriculum, procurement, privacy, and language requirements;
- Create the curriculum-graph and content-versioning architecture;
- Audit existing models for US-specific assumptions;
- Define country-specific pilot hypotheses;
- Recruit local curriculum, language, and implementation partners.

### Months 3–6: create minimum viable national editions

- Map priority curriculum units;
- Build Vietnamese, Arabic, French, English, and Kiswahili localization pipelines;
- Implement right-to-left and low-bandwidth support;
- Create teacher override and recommendation-explanation tools;
- Add offline and printable learning modes;
- Produce public-sector privacy, security, and accessibility packages;
- Configure local parent dashboards and screen-time controls;
- Test language-specific model performance.

### Months 6–12: pilot and validate

- Run limited pilots across different school and household conditions;
- Compare platform mastery with teacher and independent evidence;
- Test DTC positioning separately from school positioning;
- Measure connectivity, device, and teacher-workload effects;
- Complete local content and cultural review;
- Refine pricing and implementation models;
- Obtain required approvals and procurement registrations;
- Publish pilot findings, including limitations.

### Months 12–24: scale selectively

- Expand only the countries, grades, and subjects showing curriculum validity and sustainable implementation;
- Build local teacher communities and train-the-trainer programs;
- Add institutional integrations;
- Establish local support capacity;
- Commission independent outcome studies;
- Enable approved local content authoring;
- Continue recalibrating models with governed local data;
- Retire country customizations that cannot be supported through the modular platform.

